From 02e484de018fec1f3806b3495a26ed7408c758ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:34:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] test(host-contracts): Profile A ERC-7984 variant and TC23
 tests (lifecycle Level 2)

A local Profile A variant of OpenZeppelin ERC-7984 0.5.3 with the observer
extension (vendored test-only copy, ported by the lifecycle port script),
next to the variants without it:

- A1: setObserver(account, X) reverts if X != 0 and account is retired,
  so a retired owner can clear a thief-added observer and nobody can add
  one again. setOperator(op, until) reverts if until >= block.timestamp
  and the caller is retired: ERC-7984 operators are valid while
  block.timestamp <= until, so until == now is a grant too.
- A2: transfers to and from a retired account succeed.
- A3: a token asserting the recipient's access after granting breaks
  every transfer to a retired account.
- A4: a generic-call path refuses the registry's lifecycle functions and
  its caller-preserving multicall; without it, the path can retire the
  contract or hand it to a successor.
- Asserted residuals: the vanilla observer keeps leaking after
  retirement; a naive gate locks the thief's observer in (D22).
- Gas of the A1 gates with cold state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
